@startuml Scheduling Flow - Clubinho NIB API
!theme plain
hide footbox
title Scheduling — guarded job execution

participant "@Cron job" as Cron
participant JobRunnerService as Runner
participant ActionBoundaryService as Audit
participant "Job use case" as Task

Cron -> Runner : run(jobName, task)

alt SCHEDULER_ENABLED is false
  Runner --> Cron : skipped: scheduler disabled
else Same job is already running
  Runner --> Cron : skipped: already running
else Execute
  Runner -> Audit : open scheduled-job audit boundary
  Audit -> Task : execute task
  alt Completed
    Task --> Audit : success
    Audit --> Runner : completed + duration
  else Failed
    Task --> Audit : error captured
    Audit --> Runner : failed + duration; API stays running
  end
  Runner --> Cron : JobRunResult
end

note over Runner
  The in-memory lock prevents overlap within the enabled scheduler instance.
  Calendar and cron evaluation use the configured application timezone.
  MySQL or S3 access belongs to the concrete job, not to this runner.
end note
@enduml
